  "output": "## Code Review Summary\n\n**Mode:** specification · **Pass:** repair (CR9-1 closure only) · Candidate `ticket03-spec-r10.md`, sha256 `2f51d836…` (matches packet).\n**Files Reviewed:** 4 (candidate; r8/r9 originals; r8/r9/r10 plan-state bindings)\n**Total Issues:** 1 new (non-blocking class) + closure verified\n\n### CR9-1 closure — VERIFIED\n- **Design region == r8:** raw reads `ticket03-spec-r8.md:84-108` vs `ticket03-spec-r10.md:85-109` match line-for-line (25 lines each). Plan-state bindings agree: r8 and r10 both `0418994b…`, r9 was `e8f52791…` — the r9 drift was real and is reverted.\n- **Both annotations restored:** the r9 strings (`…CR4/CR5/C1/C2/CR7/C3 findings only`; `(F4; …no RED role — C3)`) now occur only outside §4 (lines 8, 65, 264); §4 line 108 carries the r8 forms `…CR4/CR5/C1/C2/CR7 findings only` and `` `:464-563` (F4), ``. No `C3` token remains inside the design region.\n- **Other regions match stated priors:** requirements `78bd4997…` (r8/r9/r10), tasks `5bf7c7b4…` (r9/r10; r8 `5c04a68a…`), envelope `35119699…`; AC1–AC11 identical (r9:110-125 ↔ r10:111-126); §7/§8 identical.\n- **C3 carriers intact:** §1 (line 8), AC1 (transport negative control, NO RED), T2(ii)+T2 RED sentence, §9(12), §10 row + closure table + addendum.\n- **Limits:** no shell, so digests were not recomputed; equality rests on exact raw text comparison plus persisted region bindings. Planner's delta-tool run is declared unrun (line 278); the unresolved `claims[].replacementText` is explicitly delegated to the coordinator lane (r9 convention) — not a defect.\n\n### Issues\n[CR10-1][ledger-state-drift] MEDIUM · confidence HIGH · advisory (class is outside the W09 rounds-1–2 blocking set)\nFile: `.scratch/token-efficient-tool-responses/ticket03-spec-r10.md:278`\nIssue: the delta narrative claims “Non-marker sections 1 and 10 change”, but §3 changed (line 43 adds the r10 raw-read clause; new bullet line 65; line 83 tail) and §9 changed (line 171 appends the CR9-1 scope clause). r9's own narrative enumerated “1, 3, 5, 9 and 10”, so 5 is correctly dropped but 3 and 9 are wrongly dropped. Consequence: the declared changed-section inventory omits exactly the §3 evidence bullet and §9 scope check that substantiate this closure — the declared-vs-actual invariant CR9-1 enforced, recurring for non-marker sections. Fix: “Non-marker sections 1, 3, 9 and 10 change” (or enumerate those clauses).\n\n### Positive Observations\n- Byte-exact revert rather than a paraphrase; drift narrowly localized to one line/two substrings.\n- C3 deliberately kept out of §4 while its five declared carriers are preserved.\n- Unrun delta tooling disclosed with an explicit coordinator re-scan obligation.\n\n### Recommendation\nAPPROVE\n"
